# Public discovery shell

The public site has four clear destinations: **Start** (`/start`), **Create** (`/create`), **Learn** (`/learn`), and the session-aware **Officer Hub** (`/app`). Search (`/search`) is a utility action, not another content hub. Keep language, display, and account controls separate from the primary navigation.

Use direct, descriptive links rather than public mega-menus, circular launch cards, or icon-only navigation. Keep desktop and mobile labels aligned. Mobile navigation must retain visible focus, Escape-to-close, focus return, and a keyboard trap while open. The authenticated Hub and Portal keep their own navigation.

## One public catalog

`src/lib/comms/public-catalog.ts` is the discovery registry for tools, guides, steward playbooks, Officer Learning modules, workshops, and reference libraries. Derive Create, Learn, Search, breadcrumbs, related links, and sitemap coverage from it. Keep legacy content registries only as source data where they still power existing pages. Preserve feature gates, signed-in visibility, and platform/tenant-disabled tool filtering.

Catalog copy lives in `messages/en.json` and `messages/fr.json`; do not fork public content into Markdown trees. Search and filters run in the browser over localized registry content, with query/filter state reflected in the URL. Do not add analytics or third-party search. Every card states a useful outcome, audience, approximate time, concrete deliverable, and whether work/progress stays in this browser, can optionally be copied to Officer Hub, uses Officer Hub, or is reading-only. A broad format label is not a substitute for the deliverable. Estimates remain approximate and need content-owner review.

## Start and Home

Start presents three paths: communications lead, steward, and local officer. Each path offers a sequenced checklist; selected path and manually marked progress are saved in this browser only and are not synced. Brand Kit completion is inferred from local browser state; never imply it is a union-wide shared profile. When the local Brand Kit is incomplete, recommend `/create/brand-kit` before the communications roadmap. Officer Hub remains available only when the visitor is signed in or the Hub is publicly advertised.

Learn starts with four curated task collections; active filters can be removed individually, and search terms include bilingual task vocabulary with accent-insensitive matching. Continue to test whether the flat catalog needs more progressive grouping with real visitors before adding more categories or search infrastructure.

Home has one value proposition, one primary Start action, a product preview, and a compact task chooser. Keep exhaustive channel lists and workshop facilitation details in Learn, not on Home.

## Canonical routes

| Retired path | Canonical path |
|---|---|
| `/onboarding` | `/start?step=brand` |
| `/brand-kit` | `/create/brand-kit` |
| `/tools` and `/tools/:slug` | `/create` and `/create/:slug` |
| `/guides` | `/learn` |
| `/guide` | `/learn/communications-blueprint` |
| `/guide/social-media-plan` | `/learn/first-week` |
| `/guide/steward-playbooks` | `/learn/steward` |
| `/guide/officer-learning/:slug` | `/learn/officer/:slug` |
| `/guide/workshops/:slug` | `/learn/workshops/:slug` |
| `/examples`, `/captions`, `/assets` | `/learn/library/:slug` |
| Other `/guide/:slug` | `/learn/:slug` |

Keep locale-aware permanent redirects in `PUBLIC_ROUTE_REDIRECTS`, and keep internal `Link` targets, canonical/hreflang metadata, and sitemap paths on the new routes. Query strings and fragments must survive route migration. Do not remove redirects; bookmarks and search equity are part of the product.

Privacy and security copy must distinguish Comms that stays on-device from hosted Officer Hub / Local Portal data. Do not imply Hub storage is local-only or promise that the whole platform is free forever.

## Footer

Keep the footer compact: Start, Create, Learn, What's New, Built in solidarity, Privacy, Security, Accessibility, Support, Feedback, and Install. Do not duplicate deep guide or maker links there.
